Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:46:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] docs(architecture): describe execution backends and
 model-as-a-service access

The architecture had no place for where inference instances run: the
RuntimeLauncher contract that the deployment workflow, the reconciler
and the gateway rely on was only described in the CHANGELOG, and
nothing said how ForgeMesh relates to the Kubernetes native inference
frameworks that the roadmap now uses as backends. Nor did it say where
quotas and metering are enforced when ForgeMesh serves models through
an OpenAI compatible API.

Add 10.4 (the launcher contract, the backends with their status, and
the division of work with KServe and Kthena: they orchestrate and
route on Kubernetes, ForgeMesh keeps the authoritative state,
governance and tenancy and covers environments without Kubernetes) and
11.5 (one ingress, authentication, quotas and metering enforced once
at the gateway, and placement across backends). Update the non-goals,
the layers and the overview diagram, the known limitations and the
conclusion to match.
